    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d621">

                <pb facs="0759" n="663" sameAs="frus:frus1899/pg663"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Hay to Mr.
                            Choate.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1899-09-07"><hi rendition="#italic">September 7,
                        1899</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>German Government strongly urges partition of Samoan Islands, the United States
                    to retain Tutuila and adjacent islets, and England <pb facs="0760" n="664"
                        xml:id="pg664"/> and Germany to divide the rest. The President is disposed
                    to regard this proposition favorably if details can be satisfactorily arranged
                    with due regard to the national interest and to the welfare of the inhabitants.
                    Ascertain discreetly the views of Her Majesty’s secretary of state for foreign
                    affairs.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hay.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
